[
    {
        "content": "<p>I notice that lots of LLMs when being prompted to generate a lean proof, complete the lean proof, but add a bunch of random tactics after solving the goal. I was wondering if there is a reliable way to identify which tactics are running on no goals so we can remove them.</p>",
        "id": 592851545,
        "sender_full_name": "Arnav Mehta",
        "timestamp": 1777932838
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Linters and/or lean-lsp-mcp?</p>",
        "id": 592856378,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1777935497
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I was under the impression that if you try this you already get the error \"No goals to be solved\" ?<br>\ni.e </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">ring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">--No goals to be solved</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 592869362,
        "sender_full_name": "Yan Yablonovskiy 🇺🇦",
        "timestamp": 1777941210
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks for your response, <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"773147\">@Yan Yablonovskiy 🇺🇦</span>. Do you know of ways to automatically detect which tactics are redundant and remove them. For context, I’m building an automated proving system, and whenever this issue comes up I’d like a procedure that trims away any extra tactics.</p>\n<p>Here’s an example where it’s not as simple as just deleting the tactic at which the “no goals to be solved” error is raised:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">induction</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">--No goals at the simp</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 592870495,
        "sender_full_name": "Arnav Mehta",
        "timestamp": 1777942089
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"965554\">Arnav Mehta</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/219941-Machine-Learning-for-Theorem-Proving/topic/LLMs.20adding.20additional.20tactics.20after.20completing.20proof/near/592870495\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Here’s an example where it’s not as simple as just deleting the tactic at which the “no goals to be solved” error is raised:</p>\n<p><div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">induction</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">--No goals at the simp</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span>\n</code></pre></div><br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Would that not be:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">induction</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">--No redundant tactics</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>So you remove from the end until the error goes away each time.</p>",
        "id": 592870678,
        "sender_full_name": "Yan Yablonovskiy 🇺🇦",
        "timestamp": 1777942200
    }
